  "accepted_principles": [
    "Explicit D_NOMINAL, D_PACKET, D_RECOVERY, D_DECEL and D_STOP domains; architecture acceptance does not numerically establish them.",
    "Conservative application-state uncertainty with explicit set/confidence interpretation and documented residual risk; covariance alone is not a robust bound.",
    "Continuation, renewal, recovery, conservative deceleration and stopping depend on verified feasibility; recovery has no arbitrary preference over stopping.",
    "Controller feasibility, accepted trajectory authority and physical application permission are three separate gates.",
    "Application-time and held-command checks, session/epoch identity, immutable source provenance, and cancellation acknowledgements.",
    "Causal intervention timing, mapped clocks and freshness through application and the permitted held interval.",
    "Critical fault latching, controlled reentry and explicit NO_VALID_POLICY without a false stopping claim.",
    "Numerical domains, physical response guarantees and HW01-HW10 remain subject to later characterization and review."
  ],
